{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787107642919044002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"cookable-abysmal-marmoset","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"b66b587e9a3f5563d14d104bf739a534325788e088313a3fbd4cb8eca2391f7a","event_uuid":"b249c132-8492-40da-9682-9f53bb876f96","position":{"commit_sha":"dc770143a9a76485e4020670982aacd2575d16b7","position":"1787107007614446001-b249c132-8492-40da-9682-9f53bb876f96"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d021cb3b0f2a61309909001e9eafcde506a54540fca10a8439d71719b56d96b6","event_uuid":"56b3dbc4-695c-43a1-934f-96fb8f4f0a22","position":{"commit_sha":"5c39bc765151d73b19d96e4d7ba389a4982b2a55","position":"1787107642919044001-56b3dbc4-695c-43a1-934f-96fb8f4f0a22"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787107007614446001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\nSlice C1 recorded below-seam ambient config/credential reads in the reconciler JIRA adapter/credential surface as `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`. RP-04 is not complete while these sit below the seams enforced by the in-process AST gate `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`. Parent C3a: 6633-219e-988a-42f6; grandparent C3: 075b-1479-dcb7-40ab. Disjoint file subtree from sibling C3a-CORE (ba8b).\n\nThe 12 flagged reads (path :: symbol), all drained here:\n- `access_check.py` :: JIRA_URL, JIRA_USER, JIRA_PROJECT (probe scope + probe client)\n- `adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py` :: JIRA_URL, JIRA_USER, JIRA_PROJECT, load_config (2 sites: `_acli_call_timeout` L86, `resolve_jira_settings` L119)\n- `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py` :: REBAR_RECONCILER_VERBOSE, os.environ.get (`_rebar_env` shim body)\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/settings.py` :: load_config (2 sites: `resolve_comment_max_chars` L83, `resolve_jira_datacenter_settings` L97)\n- `adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py` :: load_config (`cutover_clients` L90)\n- `adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py` :: load_config (`_pandoc_timeout` L352)\n\n(All under `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/`.) Affected SOURCE files: the 6 above, plus `src/rebar/config.py` (owned resolvers) and `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py` (removes the 12 rows).\n\n## Why the JIRA_* reads are flagged (gate mechanism — from the gate code)\nThe gate's `_resolved_env` classifies `os.environ.get(\"X\")` as owner=**credential** IFF `X` is a derived credential name, else owner=**composition**. Derived names come live from `rebar._child_env._ADAPTER_SECRET_NAMES` = ONLY the send secrets `JIRA_API_TOKEN` and `JIRA_PAT`; its comment states JIRA_URL/USER/PROJECT are *intentionally absent* (non-secret config). So JIRA_URL/USER/PROJECT are owner=**composition** env-reads, and a credential-boundary file (access_check.py, acli_subprocess.py, jira_datacenter/settings.py) owns ONLY owner=credential reads, NOT owner=composition ones. **So making them direct `os.environ.get(\"JIRA_URL\")` literals in the boundary would STILL be owner=composition → still flagged.** The correct cut routes them through an OWNED `config.py` resolver (basename config.py is a composition root that owns env-reads). The `JIRA_API_TOKEN`/`JIRA_PAT` reads here are owner=credential, already OWNED, out of scope — untouched.\n\n## Decision rule\n- **(a) CUT-TO-SEAM (default; 11 of 12 reads).** A read whose value is composed config is routed through an owned `config.py` resolver (reuse `compose_config()`/`load_config()`; add narrow named resolvers), so the ambient read moves into the composition root. Each adapter helper delegates to the owned resolver INTERNALLY (signature unchanged) — see cut details. **Preserve timing:** the JIRA endpoint + reconciler knobs resolve LIVE per operation today (env overrides file, re-read each call); the new resolvers read live per call — never composed once and threaded — so a mid-pass env override is not silently lost.\n- **(b) OWNED-IN-PLACE via `# read-via:` marker (bounded allowlist ONLY).** A read that is NOT composed config — a subsystem debug switch — stays with a `# read-via:` marker naming the category. Capped and enumerated below.\n\n### Owned-in-place allowlist (1 read = 1 marked line — the cap)\n1. `outbound_fields.py` `REBAR_RECONCILER_VERBOSE` — subsystem debug switch (`=1` emits a one-line side-car RECON record per field-diff; off by default; not in the composed config schema). 1 marked line. No other listed read is marked.\n\n## Cut details (treatment a; each helper delegates internally, unchanged signatures)\n- **`access_check.py` JIRA_URL/USER/PROJECT** (`_resolve_probe_scope`, `_build_probe_client`): read the non-secret trio from an injectable `env` mapping (default `os.environ`), live per probe. Add owned `config.py` `resolve_jira_endpoint(env=None) -> (url,user,project)` reading the env layer live (accepts an injected mapping for test parity). Both helpers delegate INTERNALLY; the `JIRA_API_TOKEN` read stays in-boundary (owned).\n- **`acli_subprocess.py`**: `resolve_jira_settings` (L119 load_config + L127-129 env fallback) → non-secret url/user/project resolution (env-over-file precedence + `InsecureUrlError` fail-loud / `ConfigError` degrade) moves into an owned `config.py` resolver; the helper delegates and appends env-only `JIRA_API_TOKEN` (owned). `_acli_call_timeout` (L86) → owned `config.py` `resolve_acli_timeout()` (same 0/negative→default clamp).\n- **`jira_datacenter/settings.py`**: `resolve_comment_max_chars` (L83) and `resolve_jira_datacenter_settings` (L97) delegate to owned `config.py` resolvers preserving FAIL-LOUD (no `except ConfigError`) and `>0 else 0=unlimited`; `JIRA_PAT` stays in-boundary.\n- **`jira_family/rich_text.py`** `cutover_clients` (L90) and **`wiki_render.py`** `_pandoc_timeout` (L352) delegate to owned `config.py` resolvers (same `ConfigError`→default fallbacks).\n- **`outbound_fields.py` `os.environ.get`**: the module-local `_rebar_env` shim serves only the single VERBOSE read; inline that read to a literal `os.environ.get(\"REBAR_RECONCILER_VERBOSE\", \"0\")` (marked, treatment b) and DELETE the unused shim — the dynamic read no longer exists (verified: one caller here; siblings have own copies).\n\nSerena `find_referencing_symbols` confirms no helper call site needs a signature change.\n\n## Affected TEST consumers (updated in-scope, run in regression)\nDrive the cut env/config through the new owned resolvers / typed config: `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/{test_config_jira_wiring,test_jira_dc_config_settings,test_config_file_wiring,test_acli_subprocess_timeout,test_rich_text_cutover,test_wiki_render_hardening}.py`, `test_dc_pat_required_heldout.py`; probe tests `tests/scripts/bridge/test_jira_capability_probe.py`. Assertions preserved; only the injection seam changes.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\nHeld-out oracle `tests/scripts/test_reconciler_jira_seam_clean_heldout.py` (imports gate scripts by bare name: `import check_config_ownership`) asserts: (i) `check_config_ownership.check(REPO_ROOT)` returns no finding whose path is any of the 6 listed source files; (ii) `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` has zero entries whose `path` is a listed source file; (iii) `# read-via:` markers across the 6 listed files total exactly **1**, confined to `outbound_fields.py` — every other listed file has 0 — so blanket-marking cannot substitute for cutting. RED now.\nBehavior regressions kept green: JIRA endpoint env-over-file LIVE precedence (a mid-pass `JIRA_URL/USER/PROJECT` override is still observed after the cut), `resolve_jira_settings` insecure-url fail-loud + malformed-config degrade, DC fail-loud, and the acli timeout clamp — via the consumers above plus `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler` contracts.\n\n## Portability\nThe gate is in-process AST with no CI-provider trigger; the cutover adds no CI dependency. Portable.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nNo stored-format or config-key changes; env/file precedence and defaults are byte-preserved. Cut-to-seam is routing/delegation; the 1 marked line is an inline annotation. Rollback = revert the change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No ambient config read remains below the seam in the 6 listed files: 11 reads are cut-to-seam through owned `config.py` resolvers (live-per-call for the JIRA endpoint + reconciler knobs) and exactly 1 (`REBAR_RECONCILER_VERBOSE`) is owned-in-place with a `# read-via:` marker; no other read is marked; the secret `JIRA_API_TOKEN`/`JIRA_PAT` boundary reads are unchanged.\n- [ ] The 12 `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows are removed and `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` passes with no path-glob exception (proven by the held-out oracle incl. its marker-total==1 / per-file-placement check).\n- [ ] The Testing regressions pass, including JIRA-endpoint live-precedence, insecure-url fail-loud, DC fail-loud, and acli-timeout-clamp; deltas noted as a comment on this ticket.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","6633-219e-988a-42f6"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"6633-219e-988a-42f6","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"a34b-4440-ad6c-4ff7","ticket_type":"story","title":"C3a-JIRA: config-ownership cutover — reconciler JIRA adapter/credential surface","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b249c132-8492-40da-9682-9f53bb876f96","56b3dbc4-695c-43a1-934f-96fb8f4f0a22"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787107642919044002,"uuid":"63fabf41-cffb-43d9-b700-3fa6a5277a18"}